      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "CUPID3D — one image in, a 3D mesh plus the camera that shot it.\n\nFirst run downloads ~7 GB of weights from hbb1/Cupid, then takes a minute or so. Peak VRAM is about 11.5 GB.\n\nTHE CAMERA DESCRIBES YOUR IMAGE\n\ncamera_info is a plain LOAD3D_CAMERA for the input image exactly as you fed it in, so wire the SAME image in as the background of Preview3D, NKD Preview 3D or Load3D. No padding, no letterbox, no reframing. It drives the NKD VFX Tools camera nodes too.\n\nHere GetImageSize reads the input so RenderMesh renders at the plate's own size and aspect.\n\nplace_on_ground drops the mesh onto y=0 so it rests on the viewer's floor rather than straddling the origin, and the camera moves with it, so the alignment holds. Turn it off for Cupid's own centred frame.\n\nInvertMask: LoadImage's MASK is 1 - alpha, so it marks the background while Cupid3D wants the subject. Segmentation nodes (RMBG, SAM) already give the subject and wire straight in. With no mask at all, rembg removes the background itself.\n\nThe mesh carries vertex colours, not a baked texture. For UVs and a texture, run it through UnwrapMesh and BakeTextureFromViews."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
